Recommend: generalized model-string normalizer for rate-card lookups (fixes agent-mcp-005's root pattern, not just one table)

Companion to agent-mcp-005 (rate-card estimateCostUsd() returns null for every real model string). That item reports the symptom; this one recommends the actual fix and provides a concrete sample set to build/test against, since a narrow patch to RATE_CARD's keys alone will just recreate the same bug the next time a model ships.

PROBLEM PATTERN (confirmed twice independently in this session, in two unrelated codebases): a pricing/cost table keyed by one exact string format silently fails against the several DIFFERENT formats a model name actually appears in across a real system - bare alias, current canonical id, dated runtime snapshot id, and whatever ad-hoc key convention the table's author picked. scratch-claude-metadata (~/dev/ai/scratch/claude-metadata) hit and fixed the identical class of bug earlier the same day (agent_analytics.py's cost estimator) via a _split_model()/_resolve_family() normalization layer that resolves any input string down to a FAMILY (opus/sonnet/haiku/fable/mythos), then prices by family rather than by exact string match. Recommend the same architecture here: normalize-to-family, not exact-string-match.

RECOMMENDED SHAPE:
```ts
// packages/agent/agent-core-provider/src/pricing/normalize-model.ts
export function normalizeModelKey(raw: string): string | null {
  const s = raw.trim().toLowerCase();
  // 1. bare alias -> current canonical family
  const ALIASES: Record<string, string> = {
    haiku: 'claude_haiku_4_5', sonnet: 'claude_sonnet_4_6' /* or _5 once added, see below */,
    opus: 'claude_opus_4_8', fable: 'claude_fable_5', mythos: 'claude_fable_5',
  };
  if (ALIASES[s]) return ALIASES[s];
  // 2. strip a trailing dated snapshot suffix (8 digits) before matching, e.g.
  //    claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 -> claude-haiku-4-5
  const noDate = s.replace(/-\d{8}$/, '');
  // 3. hyphen -> underscore, since RATE_CARD's Claude keys are underscored
  //    (but its DeepSeek keys are hyphenated - pick ONE convention and migrate
  //    RATE_CARD to it rather than normalizing inputs two different ways)
  const key = noDate.replace(/-/g, '_');
  return key in RATE_CARD ? key : null; // still null (never 0) if truly unrecognized
}
```
Call this once at the top of estimateCostUsd() instead of the raw RATE_CARD[model] lookup. Keep the existing 'null, never 0, for a genuinely unknown model' behavior - the fix is making 'genuinely unknown' correctly rare instead of the default outcome.

FULL SAMPLE SET to build/test the normalizer against - grouped by source and confidence:

**Directly verified LIVE this session (highest confidence - actually observed on the wire):**
- `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` -> should resolve to claude_haiku_4_5 (captured from a real `claude -p --output-format stream-json` result event AND from mcp__agent-mcp__usage_query's own `model` column for a real claudecli task)
- `claude-sonnet-5` -> should resolve to whatever the Sonnet-5 rate-card key becomes (seen in real usage_query rows this session; note RATE_CARD currently has NO sonnet-5 entry at all, only claude_sonnet_4_6 - that's a second, separate gap: the table itself needs a claude_sonnet_5 row before any normalizer can resolve to it)

**From this repo's own claude-api skill's authoritative pricing table (verified against skill content this session, current as of 2026-06-24):**
- claude-opus-4-8, claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-6, claude-sonnet-5, claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-haiku-4-5, claude-fable-5, claude-mythos-5 (Project Glasswing only)

**Bare aliases (how a human/agent casually fills agent_create's provider.model field - observed convention in this repo's own agent definitions, e.g. env-adoption-analyst.md's `model: haiku`):**
- haiku, sonnet, opus, fable

**RATE_CARD's own current (mismatched, internally-inconsistent) key format - verified by reading pricing/rate-card.ts directly:**
- claude_sonnet_4_6, claude_opus_4_8, claude_haiku_4_5, claude_fable_5 (underscored)
- deepseek-v4-flash, deepseek-v4-pro (hyphenated - inconsistent with the Claude keys in the SAME table)

**Inferred by pattern, NOT individually live-verified this session - flag for confirmation before relying on:**
- Dated snapshot ids for other Claude models following the same `-YYYYMMDD` suffix pattern observed on haiku (e.g. a hypothetical claude-sonnet-5-20260615) - only the haiku variant was actually captured live.
- DeepSeek's real API-reported model id format (e.g. deepseek-chat / deepseek-reasoner style vs the versioned deepseek-v4-flash/-pro already in RATE_CARD) - not independently verified this session at all; whoever implements this should capture a real DeepSeek response before assuming a format.

**Negative-control sample (must still return null, per the existing 'never silently $0' rule):**
- totally-unrecognized-model-xyz (already covered by rate-card.test.ts's own existing test - keep it green through the refactor)

Also applies to usage-plugin.ts:108's separate model-resolution path (reads provider.model from the agent's own config, a DIFFERENT code path than usage.ts:584's info.usage.model) - both call sites should route through the same normalizer so they can never drift apart again.

